4. METHODS AND PUBLICATIONS
================================================================================

The architecture and the explanation methods implemented here follow published
research. Attribution below is to the methods, not to code taken from these
authors; the implementation in this repository is the author's own except where
it calls the third-party libraries listed in section 3.

  EfficientNet
    M. Tan and Q. V. Le. "EfficientNet: Rethinking Model Scaling for
    Convolutional Neural Networks." ICML 2019.

  Noisy Student training (the "_ns" weights)
    Q. Xie, M.-T. Luong, E. Hovy, Q. V. Le. "Self-training with Noisy Student
    improves ImageNet classification." CVPR 2020.

  CBAM attention
    S. Woo, J. Park, J.-Y. Lee, I. S. Kweon. "CBAM: Convolutional Block
    Attention Module." ECCV 2018.

  Grad-CAM++
    A. Chattopadhyay, A. Sarkar, P. Howlader, V. N. Balasubramanian.
    "Grad-CAM++: Generalized Gradient-Based Visual Explanations for Deep
    Convolutional Networks." WACV 2018.

  Ada-SISE
    M. Sudhakar, S. Sattarzadeh, K. N. Plataniotis, et al. "Ada-SISE: Adaptive
    Semantic Input Sampling for Efficient Explanation of Convolutional Neural
    Networks." ICASSP 2021.

  Integrated Gradients / SmoothGrad (combined here as SmoothIG)
    M. Sundararajan, A. Taly, Q. Yan. "Axiomatic Attribution for Deep
    Networks." ICML 2017.
    D. Smilkov, N. Thorat, B. Kim, F. Viegas, M. Wattenberg. "SmoothGrad:
    removing noise by adding noise." 2017.

  CLAHE preprocessing
    K. Zuiderveld. "Contrast Limited Adaptive Histogram Equalization."
    Graphics Gems IV, 1994.

  Nelder-Mead threshold optimisation
    J. A. Nelder and R. Mead. "A Simplex Method for Function Minimization."
    The Computer Journal, 1965.


